2025-12-22 18:00:51 | INFO | Q235 id=GJ6r_T6ckc4_00-00-00_00-00-06 | pred=A | gold=C | correct=False | running_acc=61.70% | raw=The audio contains a sequence of short and long beeps, which is characteristic of Morse code.\n\nThe sequence of beeps is:\nShort-Short-Short (dot-dot-dot) - Long-Long-Long (dash-dash-dash) - Short-Short-Short (dot-dot-dot)\n\nIn International Morse Code:\n*   Three short signals ($\cdot\cdot\cdot$) represent the letter 'S'.\n*   Three long signals (---) represent the letter 'O'.\n\nTherefore, the sequence $\cdot\cdot\cdot$ --- $\cdot\cdot\cdot$ decodes to "SOS".\n\nComparing this to the choices:\nA. sOS\nB. cODE\nC. hELLO\nD. wORLD\n\nThe encoded information is SOS.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{A}$
