2025-12-22 19:05:22 | INFO | Q675 id=BV1BPRnYAEx6_00-14-34_00-14-40 | pred=C | gold=C | correct=True | running_acc=64.15% | raw=Step 1: Analyze the audio to extract the relevant numerical information.\nThe audio states: "牛排就要五多美金, 大概400人民幣, 我們如果一人一份牛排就要花掉1600" (A steak costs over five US dollars, about 400 RMB. If each person has one steak, it will cost 1600 [RMB]).\n\nStep 2: Identify the cost per person and the total cost.\nCost per person (one steak) = 400 RMB.\nTotal cost = 1600 RMB.\n\nStep 3: Calculate the number of people.\nNumber of people = Total cost / Cost per person\nNumber of people = $1600 / 400$\nNumber of people = 4.\n\nStep 4: Compare the calculated result with the given choices.\nThe calculated number of people is 4.\nChoices: A. 5, B. 3, C. 4, D. 6.\nThe result matches choice C.\n\nAnswer: \boxed{C}
2025-12-22 19:05:26 | INFO | Q676 id=BV11yrkYME4G_00-03-24_00-03-43 | pred=C | gold=C | correct=True | running_acc=64.20% | raw=The user is asking to identify the strongest acid among nitric acid, hydrochloric acid, and sulfuric acid based on the provided audio.\n\n**Step-by-step reasoning:**\n1.  **Analyze the audio for acid names and their PK values:** The audio mentions three acids and their PK values:\n    *   Sulfuric acid ($\text{H}_2\text{SO}_4$): PK is -1.3. (The audio says "硫酸的PK是負1.3" - *Liúsuān de PK shì fù 1.3*).\n    *   Hydrochloric acid ($\text{HCl}$): PK is -3. (The audio says "鹽酸是負3" - *Yánsuān shì fù sān*).\n    *   Nitric acid ($\text{HNO}_3$): PK is -7. (The audio says "硝酸的PK是負7" - *Xiāosuān de PK shì fù qī*).\n    *   *Correction/Clarification on the audio transcription:* The audio actually states:\n        *   "硝酸的PK是負1.3" (Nitric acid's PK is -1.3)\n        *   "硫酸是負3" (Sulfuric acid is -3)\n        *   "而鹽酸是負7" (And Hydrochloric acid is -7)\n    *   *Re-evaluating the audio based on the spoken order:*\n        *   "硝酸的PK是負1.3" (Nitric acid: $\text{PK} = -1.3$)\n        *   "硫酸是負3" (Sulfuric acid: $\text{PK} = -3$)\n        *   "而鹽酸是負7" (Hydrochloric acid: $\text{PK} = -7$)\n\n2.  **Determine the relationship between PK value and acidity:** For acids, a lower (more negative) $\text{pK}$ value indicates a stronger acid.\n\n3.  **Compare the $\text{pK}$ values:**\n    *   Nitric acid: $-1.3$\n    *   Sulfuric acid: $-3$\n    *   Hydrochloric acid: $-7$\n\n4.  **Identify the strongest acid:** Hydrochloric acid has the lowest (most negative) $\text{pK}$ value ($-7$), making it the strongest acid among the three mentioned according to the audio data.\n\n5.  **Match with choices:**\n    *   A. sulfurous acid (Not mentioned with a value)\n    *   B. sulfuric acid ($\text{pK} = -3$)\n    *   C. hydrochloric acid ($\text{pK} = -7$)\n    *   D. nitric acid ($\text{pK} = -1.3$)\n\nBased on the audio, Hydrochloric acid (C) is the strongest.\n\nAnswer: \boxed{C}
