2025-12-22 19:14:01 | INFO | Q823 id=BV1kt411c7QT_00-00-00_00-00-17 | pred=C | gold=C | correct=True | running_acc=65.01% | raw=The user is asking to identify the cadence of the music played in the audio clip.\n\n1.  **Analyze the audio:** The audio contains a piece of music played on a piano or keyboard instrument. The music has a clear harmonic progression and ends on a stable chord.\n2.  **Identify the final chord/resolution:** I need to listen carefully to the final chord and the preceding harmony to determine the cadence type.\n    *   The music progresses through several chords.\n    *   The final chord sounds like a tonic chord (I).\n    *   The chord immediately preceding the final tonic chord sounds like the dominant chord (V).\n3.  **Determine the cadence:** A cadence where the progression moves from the dominant chord (V) to the tonic chord (I) is called an Authentic Cadence (AC).\n4.  **Distinguish between Perfect and Imperfect Authentic Cadence:**\n    *   A **Perfect Authentic Cadence (PAC)** occurs when the V (or V7) resolves to I, and both chords are in root position, and the soprano voice ends on the tonic note.\n    *   An **Imperfect Authentic Cadence (IAC)** occurs when V resolves to I, but one or both chords are inverted, or the soprano voice ends on a note other than the tonic.\n5.  **Re-listen for detail (Root position/Soprano):** Listening closely to the final two chords:\n    *   The penultimate chord (V) seems to be in root position.\n    *   The final chord (I) also seems to be in root position.\n    *   The melody/soprano voice lands clearly on the tonic note in the final chord.\n    *   Therefore, the cadence is a Perfect Authentic Cadence (PAC).\n6.  **Match with choices:**\n    *   A. hC (Half Cadence - ends on V) - Incorrect.\n    *   B. dC (Deceptive Cadence - V resolves to vi) - Incorrect.\n    *   C. pAC (Perfect Authentic Cadence) - Matches the analysis.\n    *   D. iAC (Imperfect Authentic Cadence) - Incorrect, as it sounds perfect.\n\nThe cadence heard is a Perfect Authentic Cadence (pAC).\n\nAnswer: \boxed{C}
